Options:
1. `type Matrix [][]int` — a slice type. `got == nil` works on slices. Methods can be defined on it.
2. Define a struct with a different name and make Matrix a struct: `type Matrix struct { rows [][]int }` — but then `got == nil` won't compile... no wait, actually the test does `got == nil` on a Matrix. A struct is not comparable with nil. Therefore, Matrix must be a slice (or array/map/chan/func/pointer — but the only non-pointer types comparable with nil are slices, maps, channels, and functions). So `type Matrix [][]int` is the answer.

